{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/migration",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "migration"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "The movement of people from one place of residence to another, usually for an extended period."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "It may take place within a country or across national borders. People migrate for many reasons, including the search for better living conditions, escape from armed conflict, education and employment. Migration may be temporary, including seasonal movement, or permanent. Common forms include emigration (leaving a country), immigration (entering a country), re-emigration (returning after a temporary period abroad), repatriation (the return of citizens or their descendants from abroad with support from a state or other institution), resettlement (a state-organised transfer of people within its borders) and deportation (a legally authorised removal from a country)."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "3.9"
  ],
  "broader": {
